{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03590",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 6.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.87,
      "end_seconds": 10.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.24,
      "end_seconds": 17.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.44,
      "end_seconds": 22.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.86,
      "end_seconds": 28.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Doctor, it's not remembering the last hours. It's getting on my nerves now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.08,
      "end_seconds": 32.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.06,
      "end_seconds": 38.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Thyronorm. I take it every morning for my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.72,
      "end_seconds": 42.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.45,
      "end_seconds": 44.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "It's 50 micrograms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.12,
      "end_seconds": 49.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.8,
      "end_seconds": 77.1,
      "duration_seconds": 27.3,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, um, I really can't pin it down. I've been feeling fine otherwise too, for about four days. With feeling fine otherwise, pretty severe, if I'm being honest. Erm, I've had asking the same questions repeatedly too, for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.82,
      "end_seconds": 82.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Okay, have you had headache, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.41,
      "end_seconds": 89.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Let me think, no, I haven't had any headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 89.67,
      "end_seconds": 94.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice headache. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.94,
      "end_seconds": 107.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.14,
      "end_seconds": 118.12,
      "duration_seconds": 8.98,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Have you noticed seizure, weakness or slurred speech?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.82,
      "end_seconds": 121.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.17,
      "end_seconds": 125.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.08,
      "end_seconds": 127.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.8,
      "end_seconds": 131.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.83,
      "end_seconds": 136.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.36,
      "end_seconds": 144.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Right, have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.95,
      "end_seconds": 146.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.8,
      "end_seconds": 155.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.61,
      "end_seconds": 162.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Let me think, I have an underactive thyroid, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.91,
      "end_seconds": 168.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.79,
      "end_seconds": 176.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Hmm, I have arthritis in my knees, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.93,
      "end_seconds": 181.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.48,
      "end_seconds": 186.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.32,
      "end_seconds": 206.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.59,
      "end_seconds": 210.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "My brother has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.29,
      "end_seconds": 214.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.59,
      "end_seconds": 219.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.52,
      "end_seconds": 222.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.93,
      "end_seconds": 228.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.18,
      "end_seconds": 232.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.5,
      "end_seconds": 237.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 250.82,
      "end_seconds": 262.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse is 84 beats a minute, respiratory rate 18, pressure 108 over 77. Temp 36.8 degrees, saturation 99 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.99,
      "end_seconds": 264.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.58,
      "end_seconds": 268.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.5,
      "end_seconds": 281.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.0,
      "end_seconds": 283.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.71,
      "end_seconds": 309.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "You know who you are but not what happened this morning, and the examination otherwise is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.5,
      "end_seconds": 312.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.32,
      "end_seconds": 334.88,
      "duration_seconds": 18.56,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Okay, so my impression is this: I'd lean towards transient global amnesia. It could also be a seizure, so we'll keep that open. We should do a CT scan of the head for acute memory loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 336.77,
      "end_seconds": 342.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Doctor, I did a blood sugar before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.41,
      "end_seconds": 373.18,
      "duration_seconds": 28.77,
      "text": "Good, thanks for doing that. This usually clears in a day with no lasting effect, but we do a scan first to be safe. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. If the symptoms get worse, that's the point to come in urgently. See me again tomorrow. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.58,
      "end_seconds": 381.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Good, uh, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}